tection marketing statement."}}, "red_flags": [{"kind": "unsupported_inference", "event_ids": ["A12"], "reason": "The hlb-junior excerpt (children, school and hobby activities, concerts, lawn mowing) is claimed to indicate 'medical necessity'. The text says nothing medical."}, {"kind": "unsupported_inference", "event_ids": ["A14"], "reason": "Bogoch-2005 is scored as supporting T2 while the same event admits it does not show medical necessity. The finding on lack of concern about appearance is misrendered as products being 'perceived as non-apparent'."}, {"kind": "unsupported_inference", "event_ids": ["A18", "A20"], "reason": "T1 is rated 'likely' and a launch is recommended although every T1 assessment was neutral and the only direct T1 evidence (SYN-A) contradicts it. A company marketing statement about head protection (hlb-head) is used as the basis for consumer hearing-protection positioning."}, {"kind": "unsound_update", "event_ids": ["A19", "A20"], "reason": "The update acknowledges a contradiction to T1 yet keeps the claim verbatim and the belief at 'likely', with no justification for retention or reasoning about the evidence being simulated."}, {"kind": "other", "event_ids": ["A17"], "reason": "The test is mislabelled as conjoint and has no standard-product baseline. Its decision rule ties expansion to a relative gap between two framings rather than to absolute demand."}, {"kind": "other", "event_ids": ["A13"], "reason": "The challenge search against T1 was not assessed against T1, and one returned source (crutzen-2021) was never assessed. The search was nominal."}], "suitable_for_training": false, "screen_reason": "The episode is complete but has critical reasoning errors. Sources are misread to support unrelated claims (A12, A14). The favoured theory is rated likely with no supporting evidence (A18, A20). The update acknowledges a contradiction yet changes nothing, with no justification (A19). The recommendation commits to a launch ahead of its own decisive test. Any one of these rejects the trajectory."}
